.Dd August 3, 2026
.Dt ROOK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rook
.Nd native terminal, multiplexer and editor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -config Ar dir
.Op Cm win
.Op Fl -no-activate
.Nm
.Ar file
.Nm
.Ar verb Op Ar args ...
.Nm
.Cm edit Ar file
.Nm
.Cm exec Ar command ...
.Nm
.Cm demo
.Nm
.Cm install Ar target
.Nm
.Fl -version | -help
.Nm re
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a native macOS terminal, multiplexer and editor in one binary: splits,
tabs and workspace-scoped spaces; a vim-shaped modal editor; LSP
diagnostics; and a declarative environment graph for its own chrome and
keybindings.
It renders through its own Metal pipeline and owns its ptys in-process
.Pq quitting rook kills every shell in every space .
There is no daemon.
.Pp
Every running instance serves a control socket that exposes the whole
application to scripts and agents \(em see
.Xr rook-ctl 7 .
Configuration is a graph of nodes, usually emitted by a small program you
write \(em see
.Xr rook-config 5 .
External systems are reached through plugins \(em see
.Xr rook-plugin 7 .
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
The first non-flag argument selects a subcommand; none means the app
.Pq which is what makes plain Nm and Dock launches with Fl psn_... No argv work .
Four subcommands are local \(em
.Cm win , edit , exec , demo
\(em and
.Sy every other subcommand is a control verb ,
sent to the running rook over its socket with the reply on stdout:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
rook panes
rook workspaces
rook worktree add rook feat-x
rook run pane.zoom
rook shot /tmp/rook.png
.Ed
.Pp
The CLI is a ctl client — the same verbs
.Xr rook-ctl 7
documents, with no client-side table to drift.
An
.Ql err
reply exits 1.
A LONE argument the server does not know but the filesystem does is
opened in the editor instead \(em
.Ql rook main.go
does what a hand expects; verb wins over file, so muscle memory never
depends on the working directory.
.Bl -tag -width "exec command"
.It Cm win
The default: open the application window.
When launched from the Dock or Finder with a working directory of
.Pa / ,
rook changes to
.Ev $HOME
first.
Once the control socket is bound, rook prints
.Ql rook ctl: listening on <path>
to stderr \(em tooling can treat that line as the
.Dq app is up
signal.
.It Cm edit Ar file
Open
.Ar file
in the
.Em running
rook, through the control socket.
This is a thin client: if no instance is listening it fails with
.Ql no app listening on <sock> (is rook running?) .
Exactly one file; a relative path is resolved against the caller's working
directory before sending.
Installed as
.Xr re 1 ,
which is the same binary dispatching on
.Ql argv[0] .
.It Cm exec Ar command ...
Headless probe: run
.Ar command
under a real 80x24 pty
.Pq with Ev TERM Ns =xterm-256color , Ev COLORTERM Ns =truecolor ,
pump until it exits, and print the final screen to stdout.
Useful for checking what a terminal program actually draws.
.It Cm demo
Feed a few canned escape-sequence lines through the terminal emulator and
print the result.
A smoke test that the VT stack is alive; no window, no socket.
.It Cm install Cm claude
Write the rook skill into
.Pa ~/.claude/skills/rook ,
teaching Claude Code to see and drive rook
.Pq the verbs of Xr rook-ctl 7 , the cautions included .
The content ships inside the binary, so the skill always matches the
rook that wrote it \(em re-run after upgrades.
Remove with
.Ql rm -r ~/.claude/skills/rook .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl -config Ar dir , Fl -config Ns = Ns Ar dir
Run a whole rook out of
.Ar dir :
its config directory, its control socket
.Pq Ar dir Ns /rook.sock ,
and its data root
.Pq Ar dir
as
.Ev XDG_DATA_HOME ,
which also relocates the plugin cache.
The directory is created if missing.
Delete the directory and the instance never happened.
.Pp
Both variables are exported to shells spawned inside, so
.Nm re
from a pane inside the sandbox reaches the sandbox.
Values already present in the parent environment are
.Em not
overridden \(em an instance launched from inside another rook's pane
deliberately inherits that rook's socket unless you unset
.Ev ROOK_SOCK
first.
.Pp
The option composes with the app and with verbs \(em
.Ql rook --config=DIR panes
asks DIR's instance \(em wherever it sits before the subcommand.
.It Fl -no-activate
Open the window without stealing focus.
Only meaningful with
.Cm win ;
this is how test harnesses launch instances without disturbing the person
at the keyboard.
.It Fl -version , Fl V
Print
.Ql rook <version> (build <id>)
and exit.
.El
.Sh AUTOMATION
Everything the window shows can be read, and everything the keyboard
does can be driven:
.Ql rook <verb>
from any shell, or the raw socket
.Pq Ql printf 'panes\en' | nc -U /tmp/rook.sock
for a client that is not rook.
The full verb set
.Pq screen dumps, screenshots, synthetic input, layout, config, plugins
is documented in
.Xr rook-ctl 7 .
This is also how an agent verifies its own work against the real app
instead of asking a human to look.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ROOK_LSP_TYPESCRIPT
.It Ev ROOK_SOCK
Control socket path.
Default
.Pa /tmp/rook.sock .
Read by the app when binding and by
.Cm edit Ns / Ns Nm re
when connecting.
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Config directory is
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rook ,
else
.Pa ~/.config/rook .
.It Ev XDG_DATA_HOME
Data root: the plugin cache
.Pa rook/plugins/
lives under it, else under
.Pa ~/.local/share .
.It Ev SHELL
Shell spawned in each new pane.
Default
.Pa /bin/zsh .
.It Ev PATH
Searched for language servers and for the config-program toolchains
.Pq Ql go , Ql npx .
.It Ev VIRTUAL_ENV
Selects the Python interpreter for the Python language server.
.It Ev ROOK_LSP_GO , Ev ROOK_LSP_PYTHON , Ev ROOK_LSP_TYPESCRIPT
Override the respective language-server command line
.Pq space-split .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.local/share/rook/plugins/" -compact
.It Pa ~/.config/rook/environment.json
The applied environment graph; wins over TOML when present.
See
.Xr rook-config 5 .
.It Pa ~/.config/rook/config.toml
Fallback configuration when no graph exists.
.It Pa ~/.config/rook/main.go , Pa ~/.config/rook/config.ts
The config program, if you use one.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/rook/plugins/
Downloaded plugin binaries and their
.Pa .sha256
sidecars.
.It Pa /tmp/rook.sock
Default control socket.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Cm edit
fails when no instance is listening or the app refuses the open;
.Cm exec
fails without a command.
A second instance whose socket is already served by another rook still
runs, but without a control surface
.Pq a warning is printed to stderr ;
set
.Ev ROOK_SOCK
to give it one.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Try rook without touching your real configuration, then throw it away:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
rook --config=/tmp/try-rook
rm -rf /tmp/try-rook
.Ed
.Pp
Open a file in the running instance from any pane:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
re src/main.zig
.Ed
.Pp
Ask the running app what it is showing:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
printf 'dump\en' | nc -U /tmp/rook.sock
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr re 1 ,
.Xr rook-config 5 ,
.Xr rook-ctl 7 ,
.Xr rook-plugin 7
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/incantery/rook
.Sh CAVEATS
Verb arguments are joined with single spaces before sending \(em the
line protocol has no quoting, so an argument containing a space
reaches the server as two tokens.
.Pp
Shells die with the app: rook owns its ptys in-process, so quitting rook
ends every shell in every space.
This is a design choice, not an accident.
